@title A refused edit is a triangle with the reason in a popover, not a toast (1920x1080)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1920x1080
# T7: a refused edit (a tag with a character a tag cannot have) is a yellow triangle on the selected symbol; the reason is in its popover; it goes with the next input. No toast.
click_text "New project"
wait 20
key ctrl+k
text "place macro"
wait 5
key Enter
wait 10
# The macro window docks at the right edge; its search field is at x 1759 at this size.
click 1759 103
wait 4
text motor starter dol
wait 5
click_text "Motor starter DOL" Label
wait 10
click_text Place Button
wait 30
# Select the stop button (no problem of its own), then give it a tag a tag cannot have.
click 1100 400
wait 4
click 664 258
wait 6
double_click 1650 174
wait 4
key ctrl+a
wait 2
text "bad tag!"
wait 3
key Enter
wait 8
shot refused-edit
check_layout
# The triangle is on the symbol; its popover names the reason and offers Copy.
click 688 231
wait 6
expect "Could not rename"
expect "Copy"
shot refused-popover
check_layout
key Escape
wait 4
expect_not "Could not rename"
# The next input takes the triangle away.
click 1100 400
wait 6
shot refused-gone
check_layout
